  "implementation_notes": [
    "Do not port the old stage weighted-average scoring directly.",
    "Do not score channel count as friction.",
    "Do not treat manual work as an opportunity without importance or consequence evidence.",
    "Do not treat multiple tools as a problem without friction evidence.",
    "Use dimension recommendations as navigation aids, never as hard filters.",
    "Translate to English only after French wording is validated.",
    "Keep result generation deterministic/traceable where possible; if LLM-generated, pass only supported facts and enforce schema.",
    "Dimension selection is a simple vertical multi-select; remove applies/explore/not_yet/unknown status UI.",
    "Progress is stage-based, never question-count-based.",
    "Render explicit selection instructions for every multi-select with a limit.",
    "Group converging answers into friction clusters before asking priority.",
    "Optional free text must be collapsible/contextual and must not become required.",
    "Separate analytical result content from lead conversion UI."
